import Mathlib
import Salt.Chen.SuperProfile

/-!
# SS3a — the concrete super-solution profile: definitions + budget integrals

Design: `docs/blueprints/flags.md`, `2026-07-13 SS2`/`SS3`.  Part 1 of the 3-way SS3
transcription split.  This file records the **exact-rational-certified** piecewise-linear
profile `(Ebar, Obar)` (regenerated by `scripts/ss2_profile.py`) as honest Lean functions,
proves the definitional interface the domination panels (SS3b/SS3c) consume, and discharges the
two `∫`-budgets that `SuperSolution.massSum_le_A2_of_superSolution` /
`massOSum_le_A1_of_superSolution` require (`hEbound`/`hObound`).

## The profile

Shared grid spacing `h = 1/20`.  `Ebar` is PL on the 200 panels over `[2,12]`, `Obar` PL on
the 220 panels over `[1,12]`; beyond `W = 12` both carry the power tail `K/v³`, `K = 1/10000`.
Knots are stored as **natural-number numerators over `10⁷`** (`ebarNumList`/`obarNumList`, exact
by construction), so nonnegativity is structural and the trapezoid budget reduces to a `ℕ`-sum.

* `EbarKnots i = (ebarNumList.getD i 0)/10⁷`, `ObarKnots i = (obarNumList.getD i 0)/10⁷`.
* `Ebar v = 0` for `v < 2`, `= plVal EbarKnots 2 ⌊(v−2)·20⌋₊ v` on `[2,12)`, `= K/v³` for `v ≥ 12`.
* `Obar w = 0` for `w < 1`, `= plVal ObarKnots 1 ⌊(w−1)·20⌋₊ w` on `[1,12)`, `= K/w³` for `w ≥ 12`.

## Seam convention (load-bearing for SS3b/SS3c)

At the single point `v = 12` the tail branch wins (`Ebar 12 = K/12³`, NOT the last knot value).
Hence `*_tail_eq` holds on the **closed** `[12,∞)` (`∀ v ≥ 12`), and `*_panel_eq` holds on the
**half-open** panel `Ico (left + i/20) (left + (i+1) / 20)`.  The 200/220 half-open panels tile
`[2,12)`/`[1,12)` and the tail covers `[12,∞)` with no overlap — the clean pointwise cover the
domination panels split on.

## The interface (frozen — SS3b/SS3c consume these)

`EbarKnots`/`ObarKnots`, `Ebar`/`Obar`, `Ebar_nonneg`/`Obar_nonneg`,
`Ebar_intervalIntegrable`/`Obar_intervalIntegrable`, `Ebar_panel_eq`/`Obar_panel_eq` (Ico form),
`Ebar_tail_eq`/`Obar_tail_eq` (`∀ v ≥ 12`), and the two budgets `Ebar_integral_le`
(`∫_2^b ≤ 43/75`, `∀ b ≥ 2`) / `Obar_integral_le` (`∫_3^b ≤ 11/125`, `∀ b ≥ 3`).

Certificate (exact rationals, from `scripts/ss2_profile.py`):
`∫_2^12 Ebar = 112618127/200000000`, `∫_3^12 Obar = 34739321/400000000`; with the tail
`K/(2·12²) = 1/2880000` these give `∫_2^∞ Ebar = 126695471/225000000 ≤ 43/75` and
`∫_3^∞ Obar = 312655139/3600000000 ≤ 11/125`.
-/

open Finset MeasureTheory intervalIntegral Set

namespace Salt.Chen

-- `maxRecDepth` is raised only for the `by decide` uniform knot bound (`*Num_le`), which recurses
-- once per entry over the 201/221-element numerator lists.  No `maxHeartbeats` bump is needed.
set_option maxRecDepth 4000

/-! ## Shared piecewise-linear interpolation atom -/

/-- Linear interpolation on panel `i` (width `1/20`, left edge `left + i/20`) of a knot table
`c`, evaluated at `x`: `c i + (c (i+1) − c i)·(x − (left + i/20))·20`. -/
noncomputable def plVal (c : ℕ → ℚ) (left : ℝ) (i : ℕ) (x : ℝ) : ℝ :=
  (c i : ℝ) + ((c (i+1) : ℝ) - (c i : ℝ)) * (x - (left + (i : ℝ) / 20)) * 20


